<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55645" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατά-χυσμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which is poured over, sauce</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				535
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				1637
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βολβοὺς . . καταχύσματι δεύσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					173.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ κ. ὄξος οὐκ ἔχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philonid.
					9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταχύσματα, τά</span>, <i>handfuls</i> of nuts, figs, etc.,
				<i>showered over</i> a bride, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ κ. κατάχει τοῦ νυμφίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theopomp.Com.
					14
				</span></i>
			; also on a new slave, by way of welcome, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				768
			</span></i> (cf. Sch.adloc.), <i><span class="en">
				D.
				45.74
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάχυμα</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
